Subject: [PATCH 21/21] Read Serato track lengths, which are text like
 "05:16.81"

[AI-generated text: this description was written autonomously by an AI
agent (Claude). Review it before relying on it or submitting it.]

Serato's database V2 stores a track's length (tlen) as minutes and
seconds, e.g. "05:16.81", but the Serato feature read it with
QString::toInt(), which always failed, so every track in a Serato library
had no duration. seratoTrackLengthInSeconds() reads minutes and seconds,
hours, minutes and seconds, or plain seconds, keeping the fraction as
Mixxx's own library does; a length it cannot read is stored as NULL
rather than 0, so the column stays empty instead of showing 00:00.

Tested on Windows: a new test covers minutes and seconds, hours, plain
seconds and text that is not a length; it passes with the existing Serato
tests. On the appliance, a Serato crate on a USB drive now shows every
track's length.

[End of AI-generated text.]

